    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Created when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-i-of-leon">Ferdinand I</a> divided his realms in 1065, Castile was ruled together with León for most of its history.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-vi-of-castile">Alfonso VI</a>'s capture of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toledo">Toledo</a> in 1085 made Castile the leading Christian power and a centre of translation from Arabic.</li><li>Victory at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-las-navas-de-tolosa">Las Navas de Tolosa</a> in 1212 opened <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">al-Andalus</a>, and union with León in 1230 created the Crown of Castile.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Henry I of Castile, king at ten, died in 1217 aged thirteen after being struck on the head by a roof tile while playing with other boys at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a>'s palace in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palencia">Palencia</a>.</p></aside>
    </section>

